  "slug": "the-experiment-full-collection",
  "title": "The Experiment — Full Collection",
  "summary": "In 2019, I invited Rick Silva, Addie Wagenknecht, and artist duo exonemo (SEMBO Kensuke and AKAIWA Yae) to launch a2p (artist-to-peer), a decentralized network for artists to swap editioned digital works. The fundamental idea was for each artist to bring one artwork (edition of 10 plus one artist proof) to trade directly with others over one week. There were no financial transactions; it was an artist-to-artist system to build collections outside the traditional market.\n\nAt the time, we wrote:\n<p class=\"m-l-56 display-inline-block\">“We place this project in the tradition of artists working outside of the market. We take direct inspiration from early net.art and Fluxus. This experiment is a way for us to trade works to create a collection. Digital media has no ‘original;’ each ‘copy’ is identical.”</p>\n\nThough the term “NFT” was not used in 2019, the works were registered on the Bitmark blockchain. As Bitmark, Feral File’s parent company, retires its blockchain, these works are migrating to Ethereum. To mark this occasion, we have selected artists from the original a2p 1.0 and a2p 2.0 (co-curated with Iris Long and Carol Sabbadini) to represent the diversity of the project’s practices.\n\nThe exhibition includes:\n<p class=\"m-l-56 display-inline-block\">Alan Butler, Andrew Benson, Auriea Harvey XLVIII, Émilie Brout & Maxime Marion, hiroyuki nisougi, Kim Asendorf, LaTurbo Avedon, Lee Blalock (L[3]^2), LIA, Morehshin Allahyari, Nicolas Sassoon, peter burr, Sabrina Ratté, Sara Ludy, Sarah Rara, shawné michaelain holloway, Tabor Robak, Theo Triantafyllidis, Yoshi Sodeoka</p>",
